ursor to combine code and live data in one turn — generating a fixture from a real lookup or adding retry logic around a screening call."},"242":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor-45","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor#faq","content":"Name the tool explicitly, for example: \"Use ambriel email-lookup on test@example.com and quote the verdict.\" Agent mode with MCP tools enabled is more reliable than Ask mode."},"243":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor-46","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor#faq","content":"Keep MCP Servers enabled under Features, allow network access to mcp.ambriel.io, and update to the latest release. If tools disappear after an update, remove and re-add the server, then re-authorize once."},"244":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor-47","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor#faq","content":"Yes. Cursor supports global mcp.json and project-level .cursor/mcp.json. Use project config to pin the compliance URL per repo and isolate personal experiments."},"245":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor-48","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/cursor#faq","content":"No. Only the tool arguments you approve (such as an email or IP) go to Ambriel. Review the tool-call preview before accepting, especially in repos with secrets or customer PII."},"246":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"page","content":"Devin","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin"},"247":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-0","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","content":"Connect Ambriel to Devin AI via MCP: let your autonomous engineer query fraud scores and screening results while it codes."},"248":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-1","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#devin","content":"Devin"},"249":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-2","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#setup","content":"Setup"},"250":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-3","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"Which tools are exposed?"},"251":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-4","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#example","content":"Example"},"252":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-5","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#faq","content":"FAQ"},"253":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-6","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#next-steps","content":"Next steps"},"254":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-7","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#devin","content":"You can connect Ambriel to Devin AI via MCP with a single config block and OAuth, no API keys needed. Once linked, your autonomous engineer can query fraud scores, run AML screens, and enrich emails, phones, IPs, and BINs while it implements and tests risk workflows on its own."},"255":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-8","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#devin","content":"title: Prerequisites"},"256":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-9","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#devin","content":"You need a Devin workspace with MCP support and permission to edit .devin/config.json, plus an Ambriel account with compliance API access. Keep a browser handy for the first-run OAuth approval that authorizes Devin's tool calls."},"257":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-10","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#devin","content":"Devin suits tasks spanning many steps: scaffolding a screening service, backfilling KYB checks, or adding fraud gates to checkout. With Ambriel tools available, Devin grounds decisions in live risk data and cites real responses in its PR summary."},"258":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-11","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#setup","content":"Devin uses a .devin/config.json configuration file in your project root. Create or edit the file."},"259":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-12","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#setup","content":"Add the following configuration with the URL format:"},"260":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-13","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#setup","content":"Commit the file so every Devin session in that repo inherits the connector. Use a global Devin MCP setting instead if you want Ambriel available across all repositories."},"261":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-14","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#setup","content":"When you first use an Ambriel tool, Devin will open a browser window for OAuth authentication. Sign in with your Ambriel credentials and authorize the connection."},"262":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-15","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#setup","content":"Approve the scopes once. Devin persists the session token, so subsequent tasks reuse it without interrupting the run."},"263":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-16","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#setup","content":"The Ambriel tools are now available to Devin."},"264":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-17","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#setup","content":"Assign a concrete task to verify: \"Add AML screening to the vendor onboarding endpoint, test it with two sample companies, and report the verdicts.\" Watch the session log for aml-screen and kyb-evaluate calls before it opens the PR."},"265":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-18","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#setup","content":"You can configure MCP servers globally or per-session in Devin's settings panel."},"266":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-19","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"Devin sees the full compliance surface and can chain tools across long-running plans without further prompting."},"267":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-20","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"Tool"},"268":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-21","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"What it does"},"269":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-22","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"fraud-score"},"270":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-23","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"Scores transactions Devin creates during testing"},"271":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-24","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"aml-screen"},"272":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-25","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"Screens people and vendors in bulk onboarding jobs"},"273":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-26","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"email-lookup"},"274":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-27","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"Validates test and seed emails for deliverability"},"275":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-28","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"phone-lookup"},"276":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-29","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"Checks phone fixtures for validity and carrier data"},"277":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-30","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"ip-lookup"},"278":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-31","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"Flags proxy or datacenter IPs in abuse-handling code"},"279":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-32","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"kyb-evaluate"},"280":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-33","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"Fetches company risk profiles for review queues"},"281":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-34","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"bin-lookup"},"282":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-35","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"Resolves BINs while building payment validations"},"283":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-36","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"For audits, ask Devin to log every verdict: \"Record each screening result with entity, tool, and timestamp in the PR description.\""},"284":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-37","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#example","content":"Give Devin an outcome, not just a function — for example, backfilling screens for existing merchants or adding a blocklist check with passing tests. It will plan, call Ambriel, iterate, and summarize evidence."},"285":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-38","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#example","content":"Review the session transcript for tool inputs before merging. Devin's autonomy is powerful, but screening thresholds and block decisions should still get human approval."},"286":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-39","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#faq","content":"Use OAuth, not your password: Devin opens an Ambriel authorization page for scoped access. For shared machines, create a dedicated service identity so Devin's calls are attributed separately."},"287":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-40","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#faq","content":"Use .devin/config.json when the whole team needs compliance checks in that codebase, and global config for personal experiments. Repo config wins on conflicts."},"288":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-41","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#faq","content":"Instruct it explicitly: \"Only use synthetic fixtures, never real customer PII, and mock Ambriel in unit tests.\" Reserve live calls for integration sessions with approved test entities."},"289":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin-42","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents/devin","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents/devin#faq","content":"Yes. Ask for batched kyb-evaluate calls with retries and a CSV summary of verdicts. Start with a small batch to validate match logic, then scale up."},"290":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"page","content":"AI Agents & MCP","url":"/docs/ui/agents"},"291":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-0","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents","content":"Connect Ambriel to Claude, ChatGPT, Cursor, Windsurf and more via MCP: query live risk data from your favorite AI assistant."},"292":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-1","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/agents#what-is-mcp","content":"What is MCP?"},"293":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-2","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/agents#authentication","content":"Authentication"},"294":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-3","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/agents#available-agents","content":"Available Agents"},"295":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-4","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/agents#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"Which tools are exposed?"},"296":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-5","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/agents#quick-start","content":"Quick Start"},"297":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-6","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/agents#faq","content":"FAQ"},"298":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-7","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/agents#next-steps","content":"Next steps"},"299":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-8","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents","content":"You can connect Ambriel to Claude, ChatGPT, Cursor, Devin, and other assistants via one MCP server at https://mcp.ambriel.io/compliance. Authenticate once with OAuth and your agent can immediately query live fraud scores, AML screens, KYB profiles, and reputation lookups without manual API keys."},"300":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-9","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents","content":"title: Prerequisites"},"301":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-10","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents","content":"You need an Ambriel account with compliance API access and an MCP-capable client (Claude, ChatGPT, Cursor, Devin, or Windsurf). Setup clicks differ; the server URL is the same."},"302":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-11","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents","content":"Ambriel's MCP server lets agents call the API directly — fraud scores, entity screens, email/phone/IP checks, and KYB evaluations from inside your AI tool."},"303":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-12","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#what-is-mcp","content":"The Model Context Protocol (MCP) is an open standard that connects AI models with external tools and data sources. Ambriel's MCP server acts as a bridge, giving your AI agent access to the full Ambriel API surface."},"304":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-13","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#what-is-mcp","content":"Instead of copying data between dashboard and assistant, the model calls Ambriel tools mid-conversation and reasons over fresh JSON. You get grounded answers — \"this IP is a datacenter proxy\" — rather than guesses from training data."},"305":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-14","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#authentication","content":"Ambriel's MCP server uses OAuth for authentication. When you first connect, your agent opens a browser window for Ambriel login and authorization. No manual API key management is needed."},"306":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-15","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#authentication","content":"Tokens are scoped to your user and org, so agents inherit exactly your permissions. Revoking access in Ambriel disconnects every agent session at once."},"307":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-16","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#available-agents","content":"Claude and ChatGPT suit investigations; Cursor and Devin suit builders wiring screening into code."},"308":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-17","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"Every agent gets the same governed compliance toolset through the single MCP endpoint. The model selects tools from your wording, or you can name one explicitly."},"309":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-18","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"Tool"},"310":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-19","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"What it does"},"311":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-20","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"fraud-score"},"312":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-21","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"Scores transactions and customers with risk reasons"},"313":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-22","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"aml-screen"},"314":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-23","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"Screens people and companies against sanctions and PEP lists"},"315":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-24","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"email-lookup"},"316":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-25","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"Checks email validity, deliverability, and breach history"},"317":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-26","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"phone-lookup"},"318":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-27","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"Validates phones with carrier and reachability signals"},"319":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-28","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"ip-lookup"},"320":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-29","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"Enriches IPs with geo, ASN, and proxy/VPN detection"},"321":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-30","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"kyb-evaluate"},"322":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-31","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"Builds company risk profiles for KYB reviews"},"323":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-32","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"bin-lookup"},"324":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-33","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#which-tools-are-exposed","content":"Resolves card BINs to issuer, scheme, and country"},"325":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-34","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#quick-start","content":"One URL for all agents — OAuth handles authentication, no API key needed."},"326":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-35","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#quick-start","content":"One endpoint for every client:"},"327":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-36","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#quick-start","content":"Paste the URL into your client's MCP settings — see the agent guides above for exact clicks."},"328":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-37","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#quick-start","content":"A browser window opens on first use. Sign in, approve scopes, and return. The hammer or tools indicator confirms tools are live."},"329":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-38","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#quick-start","content":"Try: \"Screen John Doe from Germany against AML watchlists.\" A grounded answer quoting tool output means you are connected."},"330":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-39","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#quick-start","content":"When you add the MCP server, your AI agent will open a browser to authorize with Ambriel. Accept the prompt, and the connection is established. Your session is persisted for subsequent uses."},"331":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-40","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#faq","content":"Claude/ChatGPT suit investigations, Cursor suits live coding, Devin suits autonomous builds — same tools underneath."},"332":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-41","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#faq","content":"Use https://mcp.ambriel.io/compliance in production. It exposes fraud, AML, KYB, and all lookup tools behind OAuth."},"333":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-42","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#faq","content":"Yes — every call is metered under your identity and logged. Start narrow, then scale up."},"334":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-43","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#faq","content":"Revoke the OAuth grant in Ambriel account settings to disconnect all sessions, or remove the connector inside the specific client."},"335":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"page","content":"AML Compliance","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance"},"336":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-0","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","content":"Meet AML obligations with Ambriel: sanctions and PEP screening, continuous monitoring and audit-ready case management in one place."},"337":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-1","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#what-is-aml-compliance-and-who-needs-it","content":"What is AML compliance, and who needs it?"},"338":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-2","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#what-does-ambriel-screen-against","content":"What does Ambriel screen against?"},"339":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-3","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#how-does-real-time-screening-work","content":"How does real-time screening work?"},"340":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-4","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#how-does-continuous-monitoring-keep-you-covered-between-checks","content":"How does continuous monitoring keep you covered between checks?"},"341":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-5","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#how-does-ambriel-fit-with-the-rest-of-your-fraud-stack","content":"How does Ambriel fit with the rest of your fraud stack?"},"342":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-6","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#frequently-asked-questions","content":"Frequently asked questions"},"343":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-7","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#what-is-aml-compliance-and-who-needs-it","content":"Anti-Money Laundering (AML) compliance means knowing who your customers are, screening them against official watchlists, and watching for suspicious change over time. Any business that moves money or stores value — banks, fintechs, payment firms, crypto platforms, iGaming operators, marketplaces — is expected to run these checks and to prove they ran them."},"344":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-8","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#what-is-aml-compliance-and-who-needs-it","content":"Two frameworks shape almost every program. The Financial Action Task Force (FATF) sets the global standard with its recommendations on customer due diligence, sanctions screening, and Combating the Financing of Terrorism (CFT). In the European Union, the 5th and 6th Anti-Money Laundering Directives (AMLD5/6) turn those principles into hard obligations: verify customer identity, screen against sanctions and PEP lists, monitor on an ongoing basis, and keep records that auditors can inspect."},"345":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-9","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#what-is-aml-compliance-and-who-needs-it","content":"type: warning"},"346":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-10","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#what-is-aml-compliance-and-who-needs-it","content":"title: Screening is not optional under AMLD5/6"},"347":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-11","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#what-is-aml-compliance-and-who-needs-it","content":"Regulated firms must screen customers against sanctions lists and PEP databases at onboarding and re-screen them as lists change. Missing a listed person because a list updated after onboarding is still a breach."},"348":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-12","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#what-does-ambriel-screen-against","content":"Ambriel screens each entity against more than 120 sources across four list families. The table below summarizes what each family covers and why it matters for your risk decision."},"349":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-13","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#what-does-ambriel-screen-against","content":"List family"},"350":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-14","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#what-does-ambriel-screen-against","content":"What it covers"},"351":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-15","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#what-does-ambriel-screen-against","content":"Why you screen it"},"352":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-16","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#what-does-ambriel-screen-against","content":"Sanctions lists"},"353":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-17","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#what-does-ambriel-screen-against","content":"Individuals, companies, vessels, and organizations subject to economic sanctions (e.g. OFAC SDN, EU consolidated list, UN lists)"},"354":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-18","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#what-does-ambriel-screen-against","content":"Doing business with a sanctioned party can be a criminal offence and trigger asset freezes"},"355":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-19","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#what-does-ambriel-screen-against","content":"PEP lists"},"356":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-20","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#what-does-ambriel-screen-against","content":"Current and former holders of prominent public office, plus family members and close associates"},"357":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-21","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#what-does-ambriel-screen-against","content":"PEPs carry higher bribery and corruption exposure, so they need enhanced due diligence"},"358":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-22","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#what-does-ambriel-screen-against","content":"Crime lists"},"359":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-23","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#what-does-ambriel-screen-against","content":"Individuals and companies convicted of or wanted for fraud, money laundering, organized crime, and terrorism"},"360":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-24","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#what-does-ambriel-screen-against","content":"Flags counterparties with a proven or suspected criminal footprint before you onboard them"},"361":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-25","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#what-does-ambriel-screen-against","content":"Regulatory and watch lists"},"362":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-26","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#what-does-ambriel-screen-against","content":"Enforcement actions, disqualified directors, adverse-media profiles, and law-enforcement watch data"},"363":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-27","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#what-does-ambriel-screen-against","content":"Surfaces early-warning signals that do not appear on sanctions lists yet"},"364":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-28","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#what-does-ambriel-screen-against","content":"Screening runs in real time at onboarding and repeats automatically while monitoring stays switched on, so a customer who becomes listed months later still generates an alert."},"365":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-29","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#how-does-real-time-screening-work","content":"When you create an entity or call the AML screen endpoint, Ambriel normalizes the name and identifiers, searches the enabled lists, and returns scored matches instead of a blunt yes-or-no. Each hit carries a similarity score, the source list, and the matched profile, so analysts can tell a strong match from a coincidental name collision."},"366":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-30","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#how-does-real-time-screening-work","content":"Check names, companies, and counterparties against sanctions, PEP, crime, and regulatory lists in seconds, at onboarding or inside any workflow."},"367":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-31","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#how-does-real-time-screening-work","content":"Control which lists are searched and how strictly names must match in Search Configuration, balancing catch rate against false positives."},"368":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-32","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#how-does-real-time-screening-work","content":"Route scored hits into review queues, clear false positives with a reason, and escalate genuine matches into case management with a full evidence trail."},"369":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-33","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#how-does-continuous-monitoring-keep-you-covered-between-checks","content":"A one-time screen goes stale the day after it runs: lists are updated daily, PEPs leave and enter office, and clean customers can appear in enforcement actions. With monitoring enabled on an entity, Ambriel re-screens it every time the underlying lists refresh and pushes an alert when something changes — a new list appearance, a status change, or a fresh adverse-media profile."},"370":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-34","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#how-does-continuous-monitoring-keep-you-covered-between-checks","content":"Because every search and every result is written to a secure, tamper-proof log retained for 5 years, each alert arrives with its history attached: what matched, when it matched, and what the analyst did about it. That log is your audit trail when a regulator asks how a flagged customer was handled."},"371":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-35","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#how-does-ambriel-fit-with-the-rest-of-your-fraud-stack","content":"The AML API integrates seamlessly with the Fraud API, so a single customer view combines sanctions and PEP exposure with device intelligence, digital-footprint signals, and transaction risk scores. A typical wiring looks like this: score the transaction for fraud, screen the parties for AML exposure, and hold or step up anything that fails either check. Shared case management then keeps fraud and compliance decisions in one place instead of two disconnected queues."},"372":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-36","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#how-does-ambriel-fit-with-the-rest-of-your-fraud-stack","content":"type: info"},"373":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-37","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#how-does-ambriel-fit-with-the-rest-of-your-fraud-stack","content":"title: Where to go next"},"374":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-38","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#how-does-ambriel-fit-with-the-rest-of-your-fraud-stack","content":"Model the people and companies you screen in Entities, run day-to-day checks from Screening and Monitoring, and calibrate precision in Search Configuration."},"375":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-39","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#frequently-asked-questions","content":"Ambriel ingests list updates continuously and re-screens monitored entities as new data arrives — daily for fast-moving sanctions and PEP sources, on the schedule you configure for the rest. You never need to re-upload your customer base to pick up a new listing."},"376":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-40","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#frequently-asked-questions","content":"The entity generates an alert with the matched profile, source list, and score. Your team triages it in the dashboard or via the API, then clears it with a documented reason or escalates it into a case — every step lands in the 5-year audit log."},"377":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance-41","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/aml-compliance#frequently-asked-questions","content":"No. Ambriel automates the screening, monitoring, and record-keeping, but disposition decisions — clear, escalate, exit — stay with your compliance team and your risk policy. The platform's job is to make each decision fast, consistent, and provable."},"378":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"page","content":"Entities","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities"},"379":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-0","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","content":"Understand AML entities in Ambriel: how persons, companies and counterparties are modeled, screened and monitored continuously."},"380":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-1","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#what-are-entities-in-aml-context","content":"What are Entities in AML Context?"},"381":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-2","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#which-entity-types-does-ambriel-screen","content":"Which entity types does Ambriel screen?"},"382":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-3","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#politically-exposed-persons-pep","content":"Politically Exposed Persons (PEP)"},"383":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-4","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#sanctions-lists","content":"Sanctions Lists"},"384":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-5","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#crime-lists","content":"Crime Lists"},"385":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-6","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#watch-lists","content":"Watch Lists"},"386":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-7","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#why-are-entities-important-in-aml","content":"Why are Entities Important in AML?"},"387":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-8","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#how-can-you-use-ambriels-entities-feature","content":"How Can You Use Ambriel's Entities Feature?"},"388":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-9","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#how-to-create-an-entity","content":"How to create an Entity?"},"389":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-10","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#entity-fields","content":"Entity Fields"},"390":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-11","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#what-are-entities-in-aml-context","content":"In the context of Anti-Money Laundering (AML), entities refer to individuals, companies, or organizations that are subject to AML regulations. These entities can be either natural persons (e.g. individuals) or legal persons (e.g. companies). Ambriel's AML solution scans over 120 sources and continuously improves to provide the most accurate and up-to-date information."},"391":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-12","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#which-entity-types-does-ambriel-screen","content":"The four list families below cover different risk questions. Use the comparison table to decide which ones your policy needs enabled — most regulated firms enable all four and then tune precision in Search Configuration."},"392":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-13","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#which-entity-types-does-ambriel-screen","content":"Entity type"},"393":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-14","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#which-entity-types-does-ambriel-screen","content":"Who appears on it"},"394":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-15","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#which-entity-types-does-ambriel-screen","content":"Risk question it answers"},"395":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-16","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#which-entity-types-does-ambriel-screen","content":"Typical sources"},"396":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-17","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#which-entity-types-does-ambriel-screen","content":"Politically Exposed Persons (PEP)"},"397":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-18","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#which-entity-types-does-ambriel-screen","content":"Heads of state, ministers, MPs, judges, military leaders, state-company executives, plus family and close associates"},"398":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-19","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#which-entity-types-does-ambriel-screen","content":"Could this customer expose us to bribery or corruption proceeds?"},"399":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-20","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#which-entity-types-does-ambriel-screen","content":"Government gazettes, official PEP registers, commercial PEP databases"},"400":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-21","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#which-entity-types-does-ambriel-screen","content":"Sanctions lists"},"401":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-22","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#which-entity-types-does-ambriel-screen","content":"Individuals, companies, vessels, and organizations under economic or trade sanctions"},"402":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-23","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#which-entity-types-does-ambriel-screen","content":"Are we legally barred from doing business with this party?"},"403":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-24","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#which-entity-types-does-ambriel-screen","content":"OFAC SDN, EU consolidated list, UN Security Council lists, national sanctions regimes"},"404":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-25","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#which-entity-types-does-ambriel-screen","content":"Crime lists"},"405":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-26","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#which-entity-types-does-ambriel-screen","content":"People and companies convicted of or wanted for fraud, money laundering, organized crime, or terrorism"},"406":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-27","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#which-entity-types-does-ambriel-screen","content":"Does this counterparty have a proven or suspected criminal footprint?"},"407":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-28","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#which-entity-types-does-ambriel-screen","content":"FBI Most Wanted, Interpol Red Notices, national conviction and enforcement records"},"408":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-29","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#which-entity-types-does-ambriel-screen","content":"Watch lists"},"409":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-30","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#which-entity-types-does-ambriel-screen","content":"People and companies under surveillance or flagged in adverse media and enforcement actions"},"410":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-31","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#which-entity-types-does-ambriel-screen","content":"Is there an early-warning signal worth enhanced due diligence?"},"411":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-32","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#which-entity-types-does-ambriel-screen","content":"Law-enforcement bulletins, disqualified-director registers, adverse-media feeds"},"412":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-33","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#which-entity-types-does-ambriel-screen","content":"type: info"},"413":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-34","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#which-entity-types-does-ambriel-screen","content":"title: PEP screening includes associates"},"414":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-35","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#which-entity-types-does-ambriel-screen","content":"A PEP hit is not an accusation — it means enhanced due diligence applies. Always check the listed role, country, dates in office, and any family or associate links before deciding."},"415":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-36","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#politically-exposed-persons-pep","content":"PEPs are individuals who hold or have held prominent public offices, such as heads of state, government officials, politicians, or high-ranking military officers. PEPs are considered high-risk due to their potential exposure to corruption and bribery."},"416":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-37","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#sanctions-lists","content":"Sanctions lists are compiled by governments and international organizations to identify individuals, companies, and organizations that are subject to economic sanctions. These sanctions can be imposed due to various reasons, such as supporting terrorism, human rights violations, or nuclear proliferation."},"417":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-38","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#crime-lists","content":"Crime lists are databases of individuals and companies that have been convicted of or are suspected of committing crimes, such as fraud, money laundering, or organized crime."},"418":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-39","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#watch-lists","content":"Watch lists are databases of individuals and companies that are under surveillance by law enforcement or other authorities. These lists are used to identify and monitor potential security threats, such as terrorists, organized crime groups, or individuals with a history of fraudulent activities. Watch lists can be used to flag suspicious transactions, prevent fraud, and protect against potential security threats."},"419":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-40","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#why-are-entities-important-in-aml","content":"Entities play a crucial role in AML as they can be used to conceal illegal activities, such as money laundering and terrorist financing. Therefore, it is essential to identify and monitor entities to prevent illegal activities and ensure compliance with AML regulations."},"420":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-41","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#how-can-you-use-ambriels-entities-feature","content":"Ambriel's Entities feature allows you to screen entities against PEP, sanctions, and crime lists in real-time. You can use this feature to:"},"421":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-42","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#how-can-you-use-ambriels-entities-feature","content":"Verify the identity of customers and suppliers"},"422":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-43","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#how-can-you-use-ambriels-entities-feature","content":"Check for potential AML risks"},"423":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-44","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#how-can-you-use-ambriels-entities-feature","content":"Monitor transactions and activities"},"424":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-45","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#how-can-you-use-ambriels-entities-feature","content":"Comply with AML regulations"},"425":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-46","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#how-can-you-use-ambriels-entities-feature","content":"Once entities exist, keep them under continuous screening and monitoring so list updates surface as alerts instead of silent exposure."},"426":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-47","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#how-to-create-an-entity","content":"Login to dashboard"},"427":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-48","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#how-to-create-an-entity","content":"Go to Aml > Entities"},"428":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-49","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#how-to-create-an-entity","content":"Click on \"Create Entity\""},"429":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-50","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#how-to-create-an-entity","content":"Check out  example."},"430":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-51","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#entity-fields","content":"The following table shows the fields that are required to create an entity."},"431":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-52","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#entity-fields","content":"Field Name"},"432":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-53","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#entity-fields","content":"Description"},"433":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-54","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#entity-fields","content":"Required"},"434":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-55","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#entity-fields","content":"entityId"},"435":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-56","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#entity-fields","content":"Unique identifier for the entity"},"436":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-57","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#entity-fields","content":"schema"},"437":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-58","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#entity-fields","content":"The schema of the entity"},"438":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-59","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#entity-fields","content":"name"},"439":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-60","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#entity-fields","content":"The name of the entity"},"440":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-61","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#entity-fields","content":"phone"},"441":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-62","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#entity-fields","content":"Phone number of the entity"},"442":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-63","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#entity-fields","content":"address"},"443":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-64","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#entity-fields","content":"Address of the entity"},"444":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-65","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#entity-fields","content":"email"},"445":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-66","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#entity-fields","content":"Email address of the entity"},"446":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-67","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#entity-fields","content":"country"},"447":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-68","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#entity-fields","content":"Country of the entity"},"448":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-69","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#entity-fields","content":"state"},"449":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-70","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#entity-fields","content":"State of the entity (if natural person)"},"450":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-71","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#entity-fields","content":"city"},"451":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-72","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#entity-fields","content":"City of the entity"},"452":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-73","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#entity-fields","content":"dob"},"453":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-74","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#entity-fields","content":"Date of birth of the entity"},"454":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-75","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#entity-fields","content":"monitor"},"455":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities-76","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/entities","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/entities#entity-fields","content":"Monitor the entity for AML risks"},"456":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","type":"page","content":"Screening and Monitoring","url":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring"},"457":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring-0","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","content":"Protect your business from financial crime: screen entities against sanctions and PEP lists, then monitor them continuously for change."},"458":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring-1","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring#why-monitor-entities-instead-of-screening-once","content":"Why monitor entities instead of screening once?"},"459":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring-2","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring#what-are-entities-in-aml-context","content":"What are entities in AML context?"},"460":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring-3","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring#how-can-you-use-ambriels-screening-and-monitoring","content":"How can you use Ambriel's screening and monitoring?"},"461":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring-4","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring#how-do-you-triage-a-monitoring-alert","content":"How do you triage a monitoring alert?"},"462":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring-5","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring#read-the-match-before-reacting","content":"Read the match before reacting"},"463":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring-6","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring#compare-identifiers-not-just-names","content":"Compare identifiers, not just names"},"464":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring-7","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring#check-the-list-source-and-its-freshness","content":"Check the list source and its freshness"},"465":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring-8","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring#decide-clear-watch-or-escalate","content":"Decide: clear, watch, or escalate"},"466":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring-9","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring#document-the-decision","content":"Document the decision"},"467":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring-10","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring#how-do-you-switch-monitoring-on","content":"How do you switch monitoring on?"},"468":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring-11","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring#frequently-asked-questions","content":"Frequently asked questions"},"469":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring-12","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring#why-monitor-entities-instead-of-screening-once","content":"Entities play a crucial role in Anti-Money Laundering (AML) regulations. A one-time screen only proves a customer was clean on that day — sanctions designations, PEP appointments, convictions, and adverse-media stories all land after onboarding. Monitoring entities continuously closes that gap: every list refresh re-checks your portfolio, so a customer who becomes risky months later surfaces as an alert instead of a surprise finding in an audit."},"470":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring-13","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring#why-monitor-entities-instead-of-screening-once","content":"Monitoring also proves diligence over time. Each re-screen and each analyst decision is written to the tamper-proof log, giving regulators a complete story from onboarding to the latest check."},"471":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring-14","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring#what-are-entities-in-aml-context","content":"Entities refer to individuals, companies, or organizations that are subject to AML regulations. These entities can be either natural persons (e.g. individuals) or legal persons (e.g. companies). Before you can monitor anything, model each customer, supplier, or counterparty as an entity with enough identifiers — name plus date of birth, country, or address — to separate true matches from name collisions."},"472":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring-15","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring#how-can-you-use-ambriels-screening-and-monitoring","content":"Ambriel's Entities feature allows you to screen entities against PEP, sanctions, and crime lists in real-time. You can use this feature to:"},"473":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring-16","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring#how-can-you-use-ambriels-screening-and-monitoring","content":"Verify the identity of customers and suppliers"},"474":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring-17","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring#how-can-you-use-ambriels-screening-and-monitoring","content":"Check for potential AML risks"},"475":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring-18","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring#how-can-you-use-ambriels-screening-and-monitoring","content":"Monitor transactions and activities"},"476":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring-19","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring#how-can-you-use-ambriels-screening-and-monitoring","content":"Comply with AML regulations"},"477":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring-20","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring#how-can-you-use-ambriels-screening-and-monitoring","content":"Catch sanctioned parties, PEPs, and known criminals before funds move — not after."},"478":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring-21","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring#how-can-you-use-ambriels-screening-and-monitoring","content":"Re-screen the whole portfolio on every list refresh and keep a 5-year audit trail without manual work."},"479":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring-22","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring#how-can-you-use-ambriels-screening-and-monitoring","content":"Scored matches with source profiles let analysts clear false positives in minutes and escalate real hits with evidence attached."},"480":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring-23","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring#how-do-you-triage-a-monitoring-alert","content":"Every alert deserves the same disciplined pass before it is cleared or escalated. Follow these steps for each hit:"},"481":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring-24","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring#read-the-match-before-reacting","content":"Open the alert and note the score, the source list, and the listed profile. A 0.95 sanctions match on full name plus date of birth is a different situation from a 0.55 PEP match on surname alone."},"482":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring-25","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring#compare-identifiers-not-just-names","content":"Check date of birth, nationality, addresses, and company registration details against your customer record. If two or more independent identifiers agree, treat it as a likely true match; if only a common name agrees, lean toward a false positive."},"483":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring-26","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring#check-the-list-source-and-its-freshness","content":"Confirm which list produced the hit and when it was updated. Sanctions designations demand immediate action, while an old adverse-media item may only warrant enhanced due diligence at next review."},"484":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring-27","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring#decide-clear-watch-or-escalate","content":"Clear false positives with a written reason, keep ambiguous cases under monitoring with a review date, and escalate likely true matches into case management — freezing activity where your policy requires it."},"485":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring-28","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring#document-the-decision","content":"Record who decided, what evidence they used, and what happens next. The log entry is what your auditor reads, so write it for someone who was not in the room."},"486":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring-29","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring#document-the-decision","content":"Use the disposition table below to keep decisions consistent across analysts:"},"487":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring-30","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring#document-the-decision","content":"Disposition"},"488":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring-31","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring#document-the-decision","content":"When to use it"},"489":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring-32","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring#document-the-decision","content":"What to record"},"490":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring-33","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring#document-the-decision","content":"True match — escalate"},"491":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring-34","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring#document-the-decision","content":"Two or more identifiers agree, or any sanctions-list agreement"},"492":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring-35","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring#document-the-decision","content":"Matched profile, evidence, freeze or exit action, SAR consideration"},"493":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring-36","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring#document-the-decision","content":"Possible match — enhanced review"},"494":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring-37","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring#document-the-decision","content":"Partial agreement or credible adverse media"},"495":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring-38","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring#document-the-decision","content":"Extra identifiers requested, review date, risk-owner sign-off"},"496":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring-39","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring#document-the-decision","content":"False positive — clear"},"497":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring-40","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring#document-the-decision","content":"Identifiers clearly disagree (wrong country, age, company)"},"498":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring-41","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring#document-the-decision","content":"Mismatch reason, so the same alert can be auto-cleared next refresh"},"499":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring-42","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring#document-the-decision","content":"type: warning"},"500":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring-43","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring#document-the-decision","content":"title: Never clear a sanctions hit on name alone"},"501":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring-44","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring#document-the-decision","content":"If any sanctions-list identifiers plausibly agree, escalate rather than clear. Clearing a true sanctions match can itself be a regulatory breach — when in doubt, freeze and escalate."},"502":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring-45","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring#how-do-you-switch-monitoring-on","content":"Login to dashboard"},"503":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring-46","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring#how-do-you-switch-monitoring-on","content":"Go to Aml > Entities"},"504":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring-47","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring#how-do-you-switch-monitoring-on","content":"Find the entity you want to monitor"},"505":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring-48","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring#how-do-you-switch-monitoring-on","content":"Enable Monitoring switch"},"506":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring-49","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring#how-do-you-switch-monitoring-on","content":"Monitoring uses the lists and match strictness from your Search Configuration. If alerts feel noisy, tighten the score threshold or typo tolerance there rather than switching monitoring off."},"507":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring-50","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring#frequently-asked-questions","content":"Any meaningful change for a monitored entity: a new appearance on an enabled list, a status change on an existing listing, or a fresh profile that now scores above your threshold. Routine list refreshes with no new matches stay silent."},"508":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring-51","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring#frequently-asked-questions","content":"Treat PEP status as a due-diligence flag, not a verdict. Apply enhanced checks — source of funds, beneficial ownership, senior approval — and record the rationale. Only escalate to a case if you find corroborating criminal, sanctions, or adverse-media exposure."},"509":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring-52","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/screening-monitoring#frequently-asked-questions","content":"All searches and results are stored in the secure, tamper-proof log for 5 years, including every alert, disposition, and analyst note — ready for regulator or auditor review."},"510":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/search-configuration","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/search-configuration","type":"page","content":"Search Configuration","url":"/docs/ui/aml/search-configuration"},"511":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/search-configuration-0","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/search-configuration","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/aml/search-configuration","content":"Configure sanctions-list search in Ambriel: fuzzy-match thresholds, watchlist selection and entity tuning for precise, quiet hits."},"512":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/search-configuration-1","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/search-configuration","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/aml/search-configuration#what-is-search-configuration","content":"What is Search Configuration?"},"513":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/search-configuration-2","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/search-configuration","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/aml/search-configuration#what-are-the-configurations","content":"What are the Configurations?"},"514":{"id":"/docs/ui/aml/search-configuration-3","page_id":"/docs/ui/aml/search-configuration"