hone-number-intelligence#try-it-example-request","content":"Always send the full international format with the leading + and country code. Local formats without a country prefix can validate against the wrong range."},"1583":{"id":"/docs/ui/products/phone-number-intelligence-36","page_id":"/docs/ui/products/phone-number-intelligence","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/products/phone-number-intelligence#how-to-interpret-phone-number-intelligence-results","content":"A valid disposable number is the classic OTP-fraud setup: it receives codes but belongs to nobody. Allow it for low-risk contact purposes, but block it for authentication, withdrawals, and promotional eligibility."},"1584":{"id":"/docs/ui/products/phone-number-intelligence-37","page_id":"/docs/ui/products/phone-number-intelligence","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/products/phone-number-intelligence#how-to-interpret-phone-number-intelligence-results","content":"Not necessarily; travelers roam. Treat the mismatch as a review signal and corroborate with IP Address Data: a foreign carrier plus a VPN exit in a third country is far more suspicious than roaming alone."},"1585":{"id":"/docs/ui/products/phone-number-intelligence-38","page_id":"/docs/ui/products/phone-number-intelligence","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/products/phone-number-intelligence#how-to-interpret-phone-number-intelligence-results","content":"Absence of presence is weak evidence on its own, especially for new or corporate numbers. Combine it with other negatives — disposable range, no breach history for an old number, mismatched name — before declining."},"1586":{"id":"/docs/ui/products/screening-monitoring","page_id":"/docs/ui/products/screening-monitoring","type":"page","content":"Sanctions, PEP & Crime Screening","url":"/docs/ui/products/screening-monitoring"},"1587":{"id":"/docs/ui/products/screening-monitoring-0","page_id":"/docs/ui/products/screening-monitoring","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/products/screening-monitoring","content":"Screen customers against global sanctions, PEP and crime lists with Ambriel, then monitor every entity continuously for changes."},"1588":{"id":"/docs/ui/products/screening-monitoring-1","page_id":"/docs/ui/products/screening-monitoring","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/products/screening-monitoring#what-are-sanctions-pep-and-crime-lists","content":"What are Sanctions, PEP, and Crime Lists?"},"1589":{"id":"/docs/ui/products/screening-monitoring-2","page_id":"/docs/ui/products/screening-monitoring","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/products/screening-monitoring#why-are-sanctions-pep-and-crime-lists-important","content":"Why are Sanctions, PEP, and Crime Lists important?"},"1590":{"id":"/docs/ui/products/screening-monitoring-3","page_id":"/docs/ui/products/screening-monitoring","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/products/screening-monitoring#how-does-it-work","content":"How does it work?"},"1591":{"id":"/docs/ui/products/screening-monitoring-4","page_id":"/docs/ui/products/screening-monitoring","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/products/screening-monitoring#how-to-use-sanctions-pep-and-crime-lists","content":"How to use Sanctions, PEP, and Crime Lists?"},"1592":{"id":"/docs/ui/products/screening-monitoring-5","page_id":"/docs/ui/products/screening-monitoring","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/products/screening-monitoring#what-are-sanctions-pep-and-crime-lists","content":"Sanctions, PEP (Politically Exposed Persons), and crime lists are global databases of individuals and entities that pose a high risk of financial crimes, such as money laundering and terrorist financing. These lists are maintained by governments, international organizations, and regulatory bodies to prevent financial crimes."},"1593":{"id":"/docs/ui/products/screening-monitoring-6","page_id":"/docs/ui/products/screening-monitoring","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/products/screening-monitoring#why-are-sanctions-pep-and-crime-lists-important","content":"The Financial Action Task Force (FATF) recommends that countries impleme